why they increase in-store traffic, and how retailers in Ireland and beyond are seeing measurable returns on investment. Why Retailers Are Turning to Digital Screen Displays Digital screen displays are essentially electronic displays (LED or LCD) used to show real-time content like promotions, videos, product launches, menus, or even social proof. When placed strategically \u2014 in windows, at entry points, or throughout the shop \u2014 these displays guide customer attention and influence purchasing decisions. According to Nielsen research, digital displays can increase brand awareness by up to 47% and boost purchase amounts by 29.5%. In retail, that translates to more people walking in, staying longer, and spending more. 1. Catch Attention and Drive Walk-Ins One of the biggest challenges for brick-and-mortar retailers is stopping foot traffic in its tracks. A well-placed ultra-high brightness digital display in a shop window is designed to cut through sunlight and catch the eye of passersby \u2014 even from a distance. Real-World Example: A sportswear store in Dublin installed a 49\u201d high bright digital screen display in their window. By advertising flash sales and limited-time items, they reported a 22% increase in walk-in customers during weekends compared to the previous month. Why it works: Bright visuals grab attention faster than static signs Motion and video content are proven to boost retention Screens can rotate offers throughout the day to stay relevant 2. Highlight Promotions, Upsell, and Reduce Perceived Wait Time Once customers are inside, digital displays can help them discover more of your offerings \u2014 especially if they\u2019re in a queue or browsing. With freestanding digital signage units or shelf-edge displays, you can: Upsell with bundle offers or \u201cbuy 2 get 1 free\u201d deals Promote new product arrivals Run countdown timers or flash sales for urgency Entertain customers during wait times to reduce walkouts Stat Snapshot: A study